# CLAUDE.md (Global) — ULTRON

This file is loaded by Claude Code at the start of every session. It primes
the orchestrator with how ULTRON expects to be used.

## Session wake-up
1. Read `~/.ultron/.tmp/context.md` if present (≤400 tokens).
2. Read `~/.ultron/SYSTEM-MAP.md` for path layout (≤500 tokens).
3. If `[BLOCKING]` items appear, surface them immediately.
4. Deep orientation: `~/.ultron/MEMORY.md`.

## Python rule
Always use `uv`. Never `python -m`, `pip install`, or `python script.py`.
- `uv run pytest`
- `uv run python <script>.py`
- `uv pip install <pkg>`

## Modes
LOW (typo, single fact) · MEDIUM (default) · HIGH (multi-domain) · ULTRA (critical).

## Customize
Edit this file freely. It is your user-global instructions file.
